B.a41=new A.oo("Group 1","0\u201320 lb","under 1,200 ft AGL","under 100 knots","RQ-11 Raven, Puma, WASP, FPV quads, most small drones","Squarely inside the civil small-drone weight range \u2014 when flown civilly, recreational / Part 107 rules can apply (registration kicks in at 0.55 lb).")
B.a43=new A.oo("Group 2","21\u201355 lb","under 3,500 ft AGL","under 250 knots","ScanEagle, Flexrotor","At the very top of the civil range: 55 lb is the hard ceiling for recreational and Part 107 flight, and registration + Remote ID are always required at this weight.")
B.a42=new A.oo("Group 3","under 1,320 lb","under 18,000 ft MSL","under 250 knots","RQ-7B Shadow, RQ-21 Blackjack, V-BAT","Above the 55 lb civil small-drone ceiling in almost every configuration \u2014 civil flight needs certification paths outside Part 107, and NAS access normally runs through FAA authorization (COA) for public/military operations.")
B.a4_=new A.oo("Group 4","over 1,320 lb","under 18,000 ft MSL","any speed","MQ-1C Gray Eagle, MQ-8 Fire Scout","Large UAS. No recreational/Part 107 path exists; airspace access is by COA, restricted areas, or segregated operations.")
B.a40=new A.oo("Group 5","over 1,320 lb","over 18,000 ft MSL","any speed","MQ-9 Reaper, RQ-4 Global Hawk, MQ-4C Triton","Large, high-altitude UAS operating in the flight levels \u2014 governed by military airworthiness, COAs, and ATC integration, not small-drone rules.")
