B.N1=s(["Max speed: 100 mph (87 knots)","Max height: 400 feet above the ground","Near a structure: up to 400 feet above its top, within 400 feet of it","You must be able to see at least 3 miles","Stay 500 feet below clouds and 2,000 feet away from them sideways"],t.s)
B.Wc=new A.oc("This section sets the basic speed, height, and weather limits for flying a small drone.\n\nYour drone cannot go faster than 100 miles per hour. It cannot fly higher than 400 feet above the ground. There is one exception: if you are flying near a building or tower, you can go up to 400 feet above the top of that structure, as long as you stay within 400 feet of it.\n\nYou must be able to see at least 3 miles from where you are standing. And you must keep the drone at least 500 feet below any cloud and at least 2,000 feet away from a cloud sideways.",B.N1,!0)
B.Nm=s(["Before flight, learn about the weather, the airspace, and any flight restrictions","Know where people and property are in the operating area","Brief everyone involved on the plan, conditions, and their role","Check the drone works, has enough power, and everything is secure","If conditions are unsafe, do not fly"],t.s)
B.Wa=new A.oc("Before you fly, the pilot in charge has to do homework on the area and the drone.\n\nThat means: check the weather, know what airspace you are in and whether there are flight restrictions, know where people and property are on the ground, and make sure everyone helping you understands the plan and their job.\n\nYou also have to check the drone itself \u2014 that it is working right, has enough power for the flight, and that everything on board is attached securely. If anything is unsafe, you do not fly.",B.Nm,!0)
B.No=s(["Goal: stop workers from losing hearing because of job noise","At an 85-decibel 8-hour average: hearing program, free hearing tests, free protection","At a 90-decibel 8-hour average: employer must first try to reduce the noise itself","This sample covers only part of a long section \u2014 read the original for the full rule"],t.s)
B.Wb=new A.oc("This rule protects workers from losing their hearing because of loud noise at work.\n\nIn plain terms: if noise at work averages 85 decibels or more over an 8-hour day, the employer must run a hearing protection program. That includes measuring the noise, testing workers' hearing for free, and giving them hearing protection for free.\n\nAt higher levels \u2014 an average of 90 decibels over 8 hours \u2014 the employer must first try to make the workplace quieter (better equipment or barriers), not just hand out earplugs.\n\nNote: this sample covers the opening parts of a long section. The full original text has tables and more detail.",B.No,!0)
B.QG=new A.bC(B.Rx,[B.Wc,B.Wa,B.Wb],A.ar("bC<q,oc>"))
