B.m3=new A.ce("ecfr",14,"107","107.29","Daylight operation",null)
B.UI=new A.bM("Check your night setup",B.bJ,"Night flight under Part 107 needs current night training AND a 3-mile anti-collision light. If you're not sure about either, treat it as a no until you check.",null,B.m3)
B.UK=new A.bM("No flying over people",B.em,"Recreational safety rules prohibit flying over people (and over moving vehicles). One person you're filming standing still counts too, unless they are directly part of the flight crew and briefed.","Change the plan: fly where you won't pass over people.",B.bg)
B.UL=new A.bM("Take the TRUST test before you fly",B.ch,"Recreational flyers must pass The Recreational UAS Safety Test (TRUST) and carry proof.","TRUST is free, online, and you cannot fail it \u2014 you answer until you get each question right. Takes about 30 minutes, through an FAA-approved provider.",B.bg)
B.fR=new A.ce("ecfr",14,"89",null,u.m,"14 CFR Part 89")
B.UM=new A.bM("Check whether your drone has Remote ID",B.bJ,"Most drones made since late 2022 have it built in \u2014 check the settings app for a Remote ID / broadcast option, or look up your model on the FAA's declaration list.",null,B.fR)
B.UN=new A.bM("Check your airspace",B.bJ,"Near an airport usually means controlled airspace, which needs authorization. Away from airports is usually fine.","Check the free FAA B4UFLY app for the exact spot \u2014 it tells you the airspace and the max approved altitude.",null)
B.m4=new A.ce("ecfr",14,"107","107.61","Eligibility (Remote Pilot certificate)",null)
B.UO=new A.bM("You need a Remote Pilot certificate",B.ch,"Flying for work or any non-recreational purpose requires a Part 107 Remote Pilot certificate. There is no way around this one \u2014 flying commercially without it is the violation the FAA fines most.","You must be 16 or older and pass the FAA Part 107 knowledge test at a testing center. Many people self-study for 2\u20134 weeks.",B.m4)
B.UP=new A.bM("Remote ID: covered at an FAA-recognized area",B.bA,"Drones without Remote ID may only fly at an FAA-Recognized Identification Area (FRIA), within sight of the area the whole flight.","Stay inside the FRIA for the entire flight.",B.fR)
B.UQ=new A.bM("Remote ID",B.bA,"Your drone broadcasts Remote ID. It must be broadcasting from takeoff to shutdown, every flight.",null,B.fR)
B.UR=new A.bM("Registration",B.bA,"Your drone is registered. Keep the number on it.",null,B.iG)
B.US=new A.bM("Remote Pilot certificate",B.bA,"You hold a Part 107 Remote Pilot certificate. Keep it with you when you fly and stay current (free online recurrent training every 24 months).",null,B.m4)
B.UT=new A.bM("Remote ID: not required",B.bA,"Sub-250-gram recreational drones that don't need registration don't need Remote ID either.",null,B.fR)
B.UU=new A.bM("Have you taken TRUST?",B.bJ,"If you have never taken The Recreational UAS Safety Test, you need it before flying for fun. If you took it, keep proof with you.",null,B.bg)
B.UW=new A.bM("Your drone needs Remote ID",B.ch,"Drones that must be registered must broadcast Remote ID \u2014 built in, or with a broadcast module attached.","Add an FAA-declared Remote ID broadcast module, turn on built-in Remote ID if your drone has it, or fly only at a FRIA (an FAA-Recognized Identification Area).",B.fR)
B.UX=new A.bM("Registration: not required",B.bA,"A recreational drone under 0.55 pounds (250 grams) does not have to be registered.",null,B.iG)
B.Ur=new A.ce("ecfr",14,"107",null,"Operations over human beings","14 CFR Part 107, Subpart D")
B.UY=new A.bM("Flying over people has extra rules",B.bJ,"Part 107 allows flight over people only for drones that meet one of the Category 1\u20134 rules in Subpart D (weight, injury-limiting design, and an FAA declaration for most categories) \u2014 most drones don't qualify out of the box.","Check your drone's category on the FAA declaration list. If it isn't declared for operations over people, change the plan to avoid flying over anyone.",B.Ur)
B.UZ=new A.bM("TRUST test",B.bA,"You passed TRUST. Carry proof of it when you fly (a screenshot is fine).",null,B.bg)
B.V_=new A.bM("Airspace \u2014 outside the LAANC grids",B.bA,"Your location was checked against the FAA facility maps and no LAANC grid square covers it. That usually means uncontrolled airspace (Class G), where no airspace authorization is needed. Two warnings: the grids only map controlled airspace near airports \u2014 they do not show restricted or prohibited areas \u2014 and a spot right at an airport with no published grid still needs care.",null,null)
B.V0=new A.bM("Night flying needs two things first",B.ch,"Part 107 night flight requires (1) updated training or testing that covers night operations, and (2) an anti-collision light visible for at least 3 statute miles.","Complete the free FAA night-training update (if already certified) and fit a 3-mile anti-collision light.",B.m3)
B.V1=new A.bM("Night flying",B.bA,"You have current night training and an anti-collision light visible for at least 3 miles. Both are required for Part 107 night flight.",null,B.m3)
B.V2=new A.bM("Weigh your drone",B.bJ,"Weight decides whether you must register and whether you need Remote ID. A kitchen scale works \u2014 weigh it ready to fly, battery and camera included.","Weigh the drone ready to fly, then run the checker again.",null)
B.V3=new A.bM("Check your certificate status",B.bJ,"Part 107 flying requires a Remote Pilot certificate. If you never took the FAA knowledge test, you do not have one yet.",null,B.m4)
B.V4=new A.bM("Too heavy for these rules",B.em,"Both the recreational rules and Part 107 only cover drones that weigh less than 55 pounds at takeoff, including everything on board. A heavier drone needs special FAA certification and exemptions \u2014 a different, much bigger process.",null,B.bg)
B.V5=new A.bM("Check your registration",B.bJ,"Look for a registration number (starts with FA) on the drone. No number usually means not registered.",null,B.iG)
B.V6=new A.bM("Airspace",B.bA,"You're outside controlled airspace (Class G). No FAA airspace authorization needed \u2014 but check for temporary flight restrictions before every flight.",null,null)
