B.Np=s(["This weight class can be flown civilly. For the full determination \u2014 registration, TRUST / Remote Pilot certificate, Remote ID, and your flight plan \u2014 use the Can I Fly checker; Shepherd has already told you the airspace part above."],t.s)
B.W0=new A.e9("Civil (FAA) layer","REAL DATA",B.dA,B.Np)
B.B2=new A.wm(3,"block")
B.M8=s(["This location is a 0-foot LAANC grid square: no pre-authorized small-drone operations there at any altitude.","The grid is informational, not an approval or a ban \u2014 but any flight here needs manual FAA coordination (or, for military ops, the applicable airspace authority)."],t.s)
B.W1=new A.e9("Location & airspace","REAL DATA",B.B2,B.M8)
B.iX=new A.wm(2,"warn")
B.M6=s(["Group 3 and above sit outside the civil small-drone rulebook (recreational and Part 107 both cap at 55 lb). Civil operations at this size use type certification, exemptions, or public-aircraft COAs \u2014 a different process than the Can I Fly checker."],t.s)
B.W2=new A.e9("Civil (FAA) layer","FRAMEWORK",B.iX,B.M6)
B.O6=s(["The DoW source map has landed: 22 mapped entries \u2014 DoD issuances, the Groups 1\u20135 definitions, the public-aircraft / FAA COA path, and each service's stack (Air Force: DAFMAN 11-501/11-502; Army: AR 95-1; Navy: OPNAVINST 3710.7 + NAVAIR flight clearances; Marines: NAVMC 3500.107 + MARADMINs; Space Force: governed under the Air Force stack \u2014 no standalone USSF publications).","Corpus ingest from those public sources is next. Anything the map marks restricted or unread stays a titled placeholder: CAC-gated material is link-out only and is never summarized here."],t.s)
B.W3=new A.e9("Department of War publications layer","RESEARCHING",B.dA,B.O6)
B.NM=s(['All 50 states now have a researched 13-category drone-law matrix in this app (Browse \u2192 State Regulations), each with its verification date. This summary pulls your state in automatically when the location is entered as a place name (e.g. "Fayetteville, North Carolina") \u2014 raw coordinates don\'t say which state they are in.',"One caution the research keeps proving: state drone law goes stale quietly \u2014 North Carolina's knowledge-test and permit sections were repealed Dec 1, 2024 while the state still printed them. Always check the verified date."],t.s)
B.W4=new A.e9("State rules layer","RESEARCHING",B.dA,B.NM)
B.B1=new A.wm(0,"ok")
B.NN=s(["No LAANC grid square covers this location \u2014 usually uncontrolled (Class G) airspace for small-drone purposes.","Grids only map controlled airspace near airports. Restricted areas, TFRs, and local rules are not shown \u2014 check B4UFLY before flight."],t.s)
B.W5=new A.e9("Location & airspace","REAL DATA",B.B1,B.NN)
B.NK=s(["An armed aircraft is never authorized by civil drone rules or by LAANC. Live-munitions employment runs entirely through the military chain: service and DoW authorizations, weapons safety and range control, and designated restricted/range airspace (or a specific FAA authorization for the operation).","One-way attack / loitering munitions are employed AS munitions under the same principle, whatever their weight class.","Governing publications and approval authorities (from the public DoW source map): military UAS fly as public aircraft under FAA Certificates of Authorization, not Part 107 (DoD OGC determination, 16 May 2019, cited in DAFMAN 11-501 \xb61.1). Air Force: AFPD 11-5 \u2192 DAFMAN 11-501 (approval chain AF/A3S \u2192 MAJCOM \u2192 installation \u2192 squadron \u2192 unit sUAS program manager). Army: AR 95-1. Navy/USMC: OPNAVINST 3710.7 + NAVAIRINST 13034.1 flight clearances; USMC NAVMC 3500.107. Space Force flies under the Air Force stack \u2014 it has no standalone UAS publications.","Shepherd names the governing framework and authorities only \u2014 it gives no employment guidance and clears nothing."],t.s)
B.W6=new A.e9("Live munitions \u2014 Department of War rules","FRAMEWORK",B.B2,B.NK)
B.OZ=s(["This location is outside the US facility-map dataset, so Shepherd has no grid data for it. No airspace conclusion is drawn."],t.s)
B.W7=new A.e9("Location & airspace","REAL DATA",B.iX,B.OZ)
